EXAMPLE CAPTURE_FRAMES reads a count of 2 or more, INTERVAL and the tails CAMERA, MODE, LABEL in this order (PlaytestFrameCaptureTests.cs:20, :33, :63, :72; PlaytestParserTests.cs:986, :996, :1005; AI/playtest-dsl.md:367-368)
  SOURCE CAPTURE_FRAMES 4 INTERVAL 0.25
  SOURCE CAPTURE_FRAMES 3 INTERVAL 0.5 CAMERA Main MODE list LABEL run1
  SOURCE CAPTURE_FRAMES 3 INTERVAL 0.1 CAMERA scene
  SOURCE CAPTURE_FRAMES 4 INTERVAL 0.2 LABEL myClip
  SOURCE CAPTURE_FRAMES 2 INTERVAL 0.1 MODE strip
  SOURCE CAPTURE_FRAMES 10 INTERVAL 1 MODE LIST

EXAMPLE CAPTURE_FRAMES refuses a missing INTERVAL, a count below 2 or not whole (PlaytestFrameCaptureTests.cs:48, :56; PlaytestParserTests.cs:1015, :1022), a mode other than strip or list (the runner reads it as list; INTENDED I9), the tails in another order (INTENDED I2) and a tail without its value
  SOURCE CAPTURE_FRAMES
  SOURCE CAPTURE_FRAMES 4
  SOURCE CAPTURE_FRAMES 1 INTERVAL 0.1
  SOURCE CAPTURE_FRAMES 3.5 INTERVAL 1
  SOURCE CAPTURE_FRAMES 5 CAMERA game
  SOURCE CAPTURE_FRAMES 4 INTERVAL fast
  SOURCE CAPTURE_FRAMES 3 INTERVAL 0.5 MODE foo
  SOURCE CAPTURE_FRAMES 3 INTERVAL 0.5 LABEL x CAMERA y
  SOURCE CAPTURE_FRAMES 3 INTERVAL 0.5 CAMERA
  EXPECT diagnostic DECLARE_SYNTAX at 1:1
  EXPECT diagnostic DECLARE_SYNTAX at 2:16
  EXPECT diagnostic DECLARE_COUNT at 3:16
  EXPECT diagnostic DECLARE_COUNT at 4:16
  EXPECT diagnostic DECLARE_SYNTAX at 5:18
  EXPECT diagnostic DECLARE_NUMBER at 6:27
  EXPECT diagnostic DECLARE_SYNTAX at 7:36
  EXPECT diagnostic DECLARE_SYNTAX at 8:39
  EXPECT diagnostic DECLARE_SYNTAX at 9:31

EXAMPLE WAIT_CAPTURED reads a label, a mode, for the BY modes an operator and a value, then TIMEOUT and OVER in either order (PlaytestDslExtensionTests.cs:176, :187, :199, :209; PlaytestParserTests.cs:1052, :1062, :1071, :1086; AI/playtest-dsl.md:953-955, :969 for *_BY without a sub-value)
  SOURCE WAIT_CAPTURED hp INCREASED
  SOURCE WAIT_CAPTURED hp DECREASED TIMEOUT 5
  SOURCE WAIT_CAPTURED hp UNCHANGED OVER 2
  SOURCE WAIT_CAPTURED score INCREASED_BY >= 10
  SOURCE WAIT_CAPTURED cashBefore INCREASED_BY >= 1 TIMEOUT 6
  SOURCE WAIT_CAPTURED gold DECREASED_BY == 50 TIMEOUT 5
  SOURCE WAIT_CAPTURED gold INCREASED_BY TIMEOUT 5
  SOURCE WAIT_CAPTURED gold UNCHANGED TIMEOUT 8 OVER 2
  SOURCE WAIT_CAPTURED gold UNCHANGED OVER 2 TIMEOUT 8

EXAMPLE WAIT_CAPTURED refuses a missing mode (PlaytestParserTests.cs:1080), a mode that is not one of the five (the runner polls to the timeout and says nothing: PlaytestRunner.cs:443 swallows the throw of :732; INTENDED I9), a lower-case mode (INTENDED I4), a sub-value for a mode that has none (INTENDED I1) and a TIMEOUT or OVER without its number
  SOURCE WAIT_CAPTURED
  SOURCE WAIT_CAPTURED hp
  SOURCE WAIT_CAPTURED hp INCREASD
  SOURCE WAIT_CAPTURED hp increased
  SOURCE WAIT_CAPTURED hp INCREASED TIMEOUT
  SOURCE WAIT_CAPTURED hp INCREASED TIMEOUT abc
  SOURCE WAIT_CAPTURED hp UNCHANGED OVER abc
  SOURCE WAIT_CAPTURED hp INCREASED_BY >=
  SOURCE WAIT_CAPTURED hp INCREASED 5
  SOURCE WAIT_CAPTURED hp UNCHANGED OVER 2 TIMEOUT abc
  EXPECT diagnostic DECLARE_SYNTAX at 1:1
  EXPECT diagnostic DECLARE_SYNTAX at 2:15
  EXPECT diagnostic DECLARE_SYNTAX at 3:18
  EXPECT diagnostic DECLARE_SYNTAX at 4:18
  EXPECT diagnostic DECLARE_SYNTAX at 5:28
  EXPECT diagnostic DECLARE_NUMBER at 6:36
  EXPECT diagnostic DECLARE_NUMBER at 7:33
  EXPECT diagnostic DECLARE_SYNTAX at 8:31
  EXPECT diagnostic DECLARE_SYNTAX at 9:28
  EXPECT diagnostic DECLARE_NUMBER at 10:43

EXAMPLE WAIT_STABLE reads a query, DELTA, OVER and an optional TIMEOUT (PlaytestParserTests.cs:900, :911; PlaytestParser.Internals.cs:585-602; CHANGELOG.md:974)
  SOURCE WAIT_STABLE /Player|H|hp DELTA 0.5 OVER 2
  SOURCE WAIT_STABLE /Obj|C|f DELTA 1 OVER 3 TIMEOUT 10

EXAMPLE WAIT_STABLE refuses a missing DELTA, OVER or number (PlaytestParserTests.cs:921; the runner reads a bad DELTA as 0), the parts in another order (INTENDED I2) a path with a blank inside [..] (INTENDED I8) and a TIMEOUT or OVER without a number
  SOURCE WAIT_STABLE
  SOURCE WAIT_STABLE /Obj|C|f
  SOURCE WAIT_STABLE /Obj|C|f DELTA 1
  SOURCE WAIT_STABLE /Obj|C|f DELTA x OVER 2
  SOURCE WAIT_STABLE /Obj|C|f OVER 2 DELTA 1
  SOURCE WAIT_STABLE /Obj|C|f DELTA 1 OVER 2 TIMEOUT
  SOURCE WAIT_STABLE /Obj|C|f DELTA 1 OVER abc
  SOURCE WAIT_STABLE /Obj|C|f DELTA 1 OVER 2 TIMEOUT abc
  SOURCE WAIT_STABLE /[My Obj]/X|C|f DELTA 1 OVER 2
  EXPECT diagnostic DECLARE_SYNTAX at 1:1
  EXPECT diagnostic DECLARE_SYNTAX at 2:13
  EXPECT diagnostic DECLARE_SYNTAX at 3:28
  EXPECT diagnostic DECLARE_NUMBER at 4:28
  EXPECT diagnostic DECLARE_SYNTAX at 5:22
  EXPECT diagnostic DECLARE_SYNTAX at 6:37
  EXPECT diagnostic DECLARE_NUMBER at 7:35
  EXPECT diagnostic DECLARE_NUMBER at 8:45
  EXPECT diagnostic DECLARE_SYNTAX at 9:13

EXAMPLE ASSERT_CONSERVED reads SUM (or not), the names joined by +, an optional == and OVER (PlaytestParserTests.cs:940, :950; Runtime/PlaytestParserTests.cs:376; AI/playtest-dsl.md:262-263)
  SOURCE ASSERT_CONSERVED SUM /A|C|f + /B|C|f OVER 5
  SOURCE ASSERT_CONSERVED SUM /A|C|f + /B|C|f == 100 OVER 5
  SOURCE ASSERT_CONSERVED SUM item_a + item_b == CONSTANT OVER 3.0
  SOURCE ASSERT_CONSERVED SUM /Player|Health + /Enemy|Health == CONSTANT OVER 5
  SOURCE ASSERT_CONSERVED SUM a + b + c OVER 2
  SOURCE ASSERT_CONSERVED a + b OVER 5

EXAMPLE ASSERT_CONSERVED refuses a missing OVER (the hand parser reads it as 0; INTENDED I10), an OVER mistyped, a word or nothing after ==, and OVER without a number
  SOURCE ASSERT_CONSERVED
  SOURCE ASSERT_CONSERVED SUM a + b
  SOURCE ASSERT_CONSERVED SUM a + b OVR 5
  SOURCE ASSERT_CONSERVED SUM a + b OVER
  SOURCE ASSERT_CONSERVED SUM a + b OVER x
  SOURCE ASSERT_CONSERVED SUM a + b == OVER 5
  SOURCE ASSERT_CONSERVED SUM a + b == high OVER 5
  EXPECT diagnostic DECLARE_SYNTAX at 1:1
  EXPECT diagnostic DECLARE_SYNTAX at 2:26
  EXPECT diagnostic DECLARE_SYNTAX at 3:32
  EXPECT diagnostic DECLARE_SYNTAX at 4:28
  EXPECT diagnostic DECLARE_NUMBER at 5:33
  EXPECT diagnostic DECLARE_SYNTAX at 6:31
  EXPECT diagnostic DECLARE_SYNTAX at 7:31

EXAMPLE SIMULATE reads a name and the tails DURATION, TIMESCALE, TARGET, FREQUENCY in this order (Runtime/PlaytestParserTests.cs:391, :401; Runtime/PlaytestIntegrationTests.cs:512; AI/playtest-dsl.md:708-710)
  SOURCE SIMULATE physics DURATION 1.0
  SOURCE SIMULATE random_walk DURATION 60
  SOURCE SIMULATE ai_patrol DURATION 2.0 TIMESCALE 2.0 TARGET "Enemy"
  SOURCE SIMULATE wave_spawner DURATION 5.0 FREQUENCY 10
  SOURCE SIMULATE random_walk DURATION 60 TIMESCALE 2 TARGET "/Player" FREQUENCY 5
  SOURCE SIMULATE idle

EXAMPLE SIMULATE refuses a missing name, a tail without its value, a FREQUENCY that is no number (the runner reads it as 0; INTENDED I9) and the tails in another order (INTENDED I2)
  SOURCE SIMULATE
  SOURCE SIMULATE x DURATION
  SOURCE SIMULATE x DURATION abc
  SOURCE SIMULATE x FREQUENCY fast
  SOURCE SIMULATE x TARGET
  SOURCE SIMULATE x TIMESCALE 2 DURATION 5
  SOURCE SIMULATE x TIMESCALE abc
  SOURCE SIMULATE s TARGET /[My Obj]/X
  EXPECT diagnostic DECLARE_SYNTAX at 1:1
  EXPECT diagnostic DECLARE_SYNTAX at 2:12
  EXPECT diagnostic DECLARE_NUMBER at 3:21
  EXPECT diagnostic DECLARE_NUMBER at 4:22
  EXPECT diagnostic DECLARE_SYNTAX at 5:12
  EXPECT diagnostic DECLARE_SYNTAX at 6:24
  EXPECT diagnostic DECLARE_NUMBER at 7:22
  EXPECT diagnostic DECLARE_SYNTAX at 8:19

EXAMPLE TRACE_FLOW reads FROM, TO, FIELD and an optional TIMEOUT (Runtime/PlaytestParserTests.cs:436; AI/playtest-dsl.md:805-806)
  SOURCE TRACE_FLOW FROM /A TO /B FIELD Count TIMEOUT 10
  SOURCE TRACE_FLOW FROM /Player TO /Enemy FIELD health
  SOURCE TRACE_FLOW FROM /Spawner TO /WaveManager FIELD waveCount TIMEOUT 10

EXAMPLE TRACE_FLOW refuses a missing part (the hand parser reads each as empty; INTENDED I10), the parts in another order (INTENDED I2) and a TIMEOUT without a number
  SOURCE TRACE_FLOW
  SOURCE TRACE_FLOW FROM /A
  SOURCE TRACE_FLOW FROM /A TO /B
  SOURCE TRACE_FLOW FROM /A TO /B FIELD
  SOURCE TRACE_FLOW /A /B Count
  SOURCE TRACE_FLOW FROM /A TO /B FIELD Count TIMEOUT x
  SOURCE TRACE_FLOW FROM /[My Obj]/X TO /B FIELD f
  SOURCE TRACE_FLOW FROM /A TO /[My Obj]/X FIELD f
  EXPECT diagnostic DECLARE_SYNTAX at 1:1
  EXPECT diagnostic DECLARE_SYNTAX at 2:17
  EXPECT diagnostic DECLARE_SYNTAX at 3:23
  EXPECT diagnostic DECLARE_SYNTAX at 4:26
  EXPECT diagnostic DECLARE_SYNTAX at 5:12
  EXPECT diagnostic DECLARE_NUMBER at 6:46
  EXPECT diagnostic DECLARE_SYNTAX at 7:17
  EXPECT diagnostic DECLARE_SYNTAX at 8:23

EXAMPLE MOVE_PATH reads the waypoints as text up to an optional TIMEOUT; the builder reads each waypoint (PlaytestDslExtensionTests.cs:59, :70; PlaytestPositionResolverTests.cs:172; AI/playtest-dsl.md:660-661, :984)
  SOURCE MOVE_PATH 1,0,0 > 5,0,0 > 10,0,3
  SOURCE MOVE_PATH 0,0,0 > 5,0,5 > 10,0,0 TIMEOUT 8
  SOURCE MOVE_PATH 0,0,0 > @/A.position > 5,0,5
  SOURCE MOVE_PATH $start > $end > $start

EXAMPLE MOVE_PATH refuses a line without a waypoint, a TIMEOUT without a number and a token after the number
  SOURCE MOVE_PATH
  SOURCE MOVE_PATH 1,0,0 > 5,0,0 TIMEOUT
  SOURCE MOVE_PATH 1,0,0 > 5,0,0 TIMEOUT abc
  SOURCE MOVE_PATH 1,0,0 > 5,0,0 TIMEOUT 8 9
  EXPECT diagnostic DECLARE_SYNTAX at 1:1
  EXPECT diagnostic DECLARE_SYNTAX at 2:25
  EXPECT diagnostic DECLARE_NUMBER at 3:33
  EXPECT diagnostic DECLARE_SYNTAX at 4:35

EXAMPLE a name, a camera, a label or a field with a blank is written in quotes (PlaytestParser.Subroutines.cs:503-523)
  SOURCE CAPTURE_FRAMES 3 INTERVAL 0.5 CAMERA "Main Camera" LABEL "my clip"
  SOURCE WAIT_CAPTURED "my label" INCREASED
  SOURCE SIMULATE "random walk" DURATION 5
  SOURCE TRACE_FLOW FROM /A TO /B FIELD "my field"
